        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(hooks): bound HOOK.md reads during hook install validation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`resolveHookNameFromDir` in `src/hooks/install.ts` reads `HOOK.md` with an unbounded `fs.promises.readFile` call. A malicious or malformed hook package containing a multi-gigabyte `HOOK.md` could force the install path to buffer the entire file into memory just to extract the hook name from frontmatter, leading to OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`HOOK.md` is only parsed for a short frontmatter block (name, description). A 1 MiB cap is generous headroom for legitimate hook documentation while preventing the install path from being used as a memory exhaustion vector.\n\n## User Impact\n\nInstalling a hook package with an oversized `HOOK.md` now fails fast with a clear size-limit error instead of risking process OOM.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a regression test that writes a `1 MiB + 1` byte `HOOK.md` and asserts `installHooksFromPath` rejects with `File exceeds 1048576 bytes`.\n- Local focused run: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/hooks/install.test.ts --run` passes (29/29 tests).\n\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nI created a local hook directory with a `1 MiB + 1` byte `HOOK.md` and ran the regression test that exercises `installHooksFromPath`. The install path rejects the oversized file before parsing frontmatter:\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/hooks/install.test.ts --run\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.hooks.config.ts\n RUN  v4.1.9\n ✓ |hooks| src/hooks/install.test.ts (29 tests) 2510ms\n     ✓ rejects an oversized HOOK.md to prevent OOM during frontmatter parsing\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  29 passed (29)\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 15.11s\n```\n\nThe oversized `HOOK.md` test fails with `File exceeds 1048576 bytes`, confirming the bounded read is enforced before frontmatter parsing and no downstream install steps run.",
